        {
            "collapsed": false,
            "id": "7767e1d8a2",
            "info": "Life is a system of chemical replicators composed of cells. It reproduces using DNA replication and is encapsulated in phospholipid membranes.",
            "name": "Life"
        },
        {
            "collapsed": false,
            "id": "c7bc58519b",
            "info": "Bacteria are single-celled organisms, and one of the two primary divisions of life on Earth.",
            "name": "Bacteria",
            "parent": "7767e1d8a2"
        },
        {
            "collapsed": false,
            "id": "a4a8941edb",
            "info": "Also known as terrabacteria",
            "name": "Bacillati",
            "parent": "c7bc58519b"
        },
        {
            "collapsed": false,
            "id": "d8a0ddce66",
            "info": "The clade which devloped oxygenic photosynthesis. While other clades use sunlight to drive other reactions, cyanobacteria are the only to use sunlight split water, using the electrons and protons from hydrogen to power the enzyme complexes which combine carbon dioxide into sugars, releasing oxygen as a byproduct. All other clades which use this process get it by culturing internal populations of cyanobacteria, typically as endosymbiotic chloroplasts, sometimes as trapped free-living populations, and sometimes as endosymbiotes of trapped free-living populations.",
            "name": "Cyanobacteria",
            "parent": "a4a8941edb"
        },
        {
            "collapsed": false,
            "id": "d7d569aa04",
