        {
            "collapsed": false,
            "id": "2f18e7b0ba",
            "info": "Mitochondria are obligate intracellular endosymbiotes of almost all modern eukaryotes, and are vitally important in the evolution of the same. Their ancestral traits are highly reduced after millions of years of coevolution within their hosts, and they can no longer live alone. They have now become as intrinsic parts of the soma of their host cells, called organelles.",
            "name": "Mitochondria",
            "parent": "374e90eb98"
        },
