        {
            "collapsed": false,
            "id": "49aaf051e1",
            "info": "Cells with a nucleus. Once believed to be equally-related to bacteria and archaea, it is now understood to be nested within the archaea, although it is still disputed whether eukarya diversed within the heimdallarchaeia or as sister to it. The acquisition of endosymbiotic mitochondria from formerly free-living bacteria by the ancestral archaeote is believed to have driven the early development of the clade, and influecned its metabolism and membrane dynamics through the adoption of bacterial machinery.",
