        {
            "collapsed": false,
            "id": "3a0f8b3061",
            "info": "An extremely diverse clade of multicellular eukaryotes. In most members, nutrients are aquired through photosynthesis, although some parasitic species and clades siphon nutrients instead. Plants were pivotal in the migration of some life to land, as the first to colonize it, and generally among the lowest levels of nutrient producers for the complex food webs that sustain land ecologies. Many species and clades of plants have various types of symbiotic relationships with bacteria, fungi, animals, and other plants.",
